# Architecture

Monorepo (npm workspaces): `backend` (Express 5 + TS + Prisma 6 + PostgreSQL 16)
and `frontend` (Next.js 15 App Router + TS + Tailwind CSS 4 + Zustand 5).

- Backend layering (strict order, never skip layers):
  `routers/ (route + zod validation middleware) → controllers/ (HTTP only) →
  services/ (business logic) → models/ (Prisma data access)`.
  `proxy/` holds outbound integrations (AI try-on, WhatsApp). `middleware/`
  holds auth, roles, rate limits, error handling. `utils/` is pure functions only.
- Frontend layering: `app/` pages stay thin; rendering lives in
  `components/`; data fetching in `hooks/`; pure logic in `helpers/`;
  client state in `store/` (Zustand); strings in `i18n/en.ts` + `i18n/ur.ts`.
- The API contract is `docs/api-contract.md` — backend and frontend must match
  it exactly (envelope `{ success, data }` / `{ success:false, error }`).
- Order status flow is locked: PLACED → ACCEPTED → MEASUREMENTS_CONFIRMED →
  STITCHING → QUALITY_CHECK → READY → DELIVERED, plus CANCELLED. Never skip
  states. Rules live in `backend/src/utils/status.ts`.
- Server recalculates all money; the frontend only mirrors prices for display.
